{:doc ["New-DSL conversion of ac/vfx/effects/blood_retrograde_charge.edn (S6)."
        "Old file at ac/vfx/effects/blood_retrograde_charge.edn left untouched,"
        "same convention as S6's ability conversions (ac/skills/*.edn siblings"
        "of ac/combat/abilities/*.edn)."
        ""
        ":vfx/charge-slow has NO case in cn.li.vfx.final-engine/sample-node --"
        "grep-confirmed, the full case list is :vfx/let :vfx/repeat :vfx/"
        "timeline :vfx/group :vfx/branch :vfx/fade :vfx/ring :vfx/beam :vfx/"
        "ray-beam :vfx/line :vfx/quad :vfx/emitter :vfx/audio :vfx/audio-one-"
        "shot :vfx/audio-loop :vfx/camera :vfx/camera-fov :vfx/camera-shake"
        ":vfx/post-process, plus a default fallback that wraps any other"
        "\"vfx\"-namespaced component into a :typed-vfx quad op the redesign"
        "plan documents as ALSO unrenderable (deletion list item \":typed-vfx"
        "运行期回退\"). So :vfx/charge-slow never produced a single real pixel"
        "in the old engine either -- this is the SAME \"referenced but never"
        "actually implemented anywhere\" gap class the ability conversion hit"
        "repeatedly (:vec3/launch, :value/status-id, ...), just discovered on"
        "the VFX side instead of the language-kernel side. There is nothing to"
        "faithfully preserve, so the new :scene is an honest empty program,"
        "not an invented replacement design (that would be new creative work"
        "outside this refactor's scope: \"不保留旧设计、不兼容旧代码...验收标准"
        "为「能加载、能编译通过」\")."
        ""
        "The old top-level :bounds key (here: none, this file never had one)"
        "and :control-graph's structural :vfx/timeline wrapper have no"
        "analogue in the new document shape: audience/network culling is now"
        "supplied by the CALLER at the vfx! call site (:audience {...} on each"
        "ability's own vfx! invocation), not declared per-effect, and a scene"
        "is just a flat :do sequence re-sampled every frame -- no :control-"
        "graph/:bounds split needed. :asset/type, :asset/version, :inputs,"
        ":state-slots kept byte-for-byte; only :control-graph is replaced by"
        ":scene."]
 :schema-version 2
 :kind :vfx/system
 :asset/type :vfx/system
 :asset/version 1
 :id :blood-retrograde-charge
 :revision 1
 :lifecycle :session
 :inputs {:spawn {:speed :float}
          :update {:speed {:type :float}}
          :destroy {}}
 :state-slots {:age :float :seed :int}
 :scene
 "{:ability :blood-retrograde-charge
   :do [(finish {:outcome :performed})]}"}
